- Story & Context: On the gravel rooftop of the compressor station above Tunnel-7, amateur astronomer Marta taped a cracked eyepiece to an uncoiled cardboard mailing tube and pointed it directly at the gas giant, only for a power spike from the unauthorized concert below to blow out the neighborhood's grid. The sudden blackout left the rooftop in shocking darkness, revealing not only the planet's moons but the blue corona of an electrical fire racing down the exterior grounding cables into the club entrance. Inside, Karoline saw the sparks burst through the concrete ceiling and kicked her fuzz pedal into a blind, screaming tempo while the choir matched the pitch of the arc: "we point the lens until the sky goes red."
